#
# Source: "Linked Web Storage Protocol 1.0", W3C Working Draft 19 October 2026
#   this-version: https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/
#   snapshot:     catalog/sources/WD-lws10-core-20261019.html
# Extraction:     tools/extractor/extract_clauses.py (216 normative blocks total)
# Hashes:         tools/extractor/clause_hash.py, rule per DECISIONS.md D-0008
#
# Gate 1 closed 2026-07-16: the hand-curated seeds below are approved by Erich
# (status touchstone:Approved). The mass extraction of the remaining core-draft
# clauses follows them (status touchstone:Draft pending batch review); entries are
# generated by tools/extractor/emit_candidates.py from the curation file in
# catalog/sources/.
#
# Re-baselined 2026-09-02 from the 22 June 2026 WD onto this draft (DECISIONS.md
# D-0037/D-0040). Twenty clauses no longer appear in the spec: six kept their slug
# with new text, thirteen were replaced by successors, and one (Slug handling) is
# gone outright. Forty-nine clauses are new, twenty-nine of them the Notifications
# section the June draft did not have.
#
# Re-baselined 2026-09-30 onto the 21 September 2026 WD (DECISIONS.md D-0057). Thirteen
# normative blocks changed: the 428-on-unconditional-PUT and parent-ETag-after-delete
# MUSTs are gone, conditional requests went from MUST to SHOULD, the ETag on a 201 and
# the new-ETag-after-update SHOULD are gone, linksets keep only the 412 MUST, and the
# authorization server metadata gained subject_identifier_types_supported.
#
# Re-baselined 2026-10-05 onto the 5 October 2026 WD (DECISIONS.md D-0086). Three normative
# blocks changed, all to name JSON Patch (RFC 6902) as the baseline patch format where they
# named JSON Merge Patch (w3c/lws-protocol#255): two Approved seeds are retired and have
# Draft successors, and the linkset PATCH entry is renamed for the new format.
#
# Re-baselined 2026-10-19 onto the 19 October 2026 WD (DECISIONS.md D-0100). A 401's
# challenge now carries the RFC 9728 resource_metadata parameter in place of as_uri and
# realm, with a Link to the storage, which is the token request's resource and the access
# token's audience (w3c/lws-protocol#256). Content negotiation requires only
# application/lws+json on containers, and a representation asked for in the LWS profile
# must be RDF isomorphic to it (#253): the Approved seed conneg-media-type-equivalence is
# retired, with a Draft successor. A new section lets servers move resources between
# containers by patching the up link (#237). The module grows from 190 requirements to 215.

